  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will support the Dominica Public Service Union (DPSU), Waterfront and Allied Workers Union (WAWU), and Dominica Amalgamated Workers Union (DAWU) in establishing a trade union federation. This support will involve facilitating their collaboration, providing inputs and guidance on the process, and sharing best practices from other countries. The aim is to strengthen the trade union movement in Dominica, enhancing their collective bargaining power and representation.

By coming together under one umbrella organization, these trade unions will benefit from increased unity and effectiveness in addressing labour issues. The ILO&apos;s assistance will help ensure a smooth and successful establishment of the Trade Union Centre (TUC), benefiting the members of DPSU, WAWU, and DAWU, as well as the broader workforce in Dominica.</narrative>
  </description>
